sn't sound obtuse, but it's what I'm actually doing and what's actually helping. And it's so easy to fucking use this as a bypass, but I'm going to say it anyway. What I will do is when I notice I'm getting caught in the swirl of agitation and for me, that means because I'm a codependent person, I start trying to manipulate the energies of everyone in a way where everyone can like understand each other and get along. When I catch myself doing that, I will first go to the silence. Now, it's very easy to use that as a bypass where I'm checking out from everyone, but instead what it feels like is, so when I say go to the silence, what I mean is right now people are listening to my words and we're all used to hearing the sounds and the sounds exist. And the example that I give people in my meditation classes a lot because I'm an artist is we talk in drawings about positive space and negative space. So there's a white piece of paper and then you grab an ink brush and you start painting on the piece of paper. The negative space is the white piece of paper, the positive space is the ink mark you've just made, the sounds are the positive space and there's still the negative space. I just stopped talking. There it was. There's the quiet that the sounds come out of. So it's not woo woo and mystical, it's just that there's both. There's sound and quiet. And when somebody's talking, there is also this quiet that's happening that the sounds are emerging out of. And I don't need to make this complicated, but there's just this way where when I connect with it, it feels like my body softens. So people can also just do this in a somatic way. Feel your weight in the chair, feel the seat that you're in, notice your breath. These are all just ways to come to awareness, right? So whatever works for you, if you have a meditation practice, come to awareness. What I noticed then is that I, the thing that emerges to the foreground, instead of me being in controller mode, is love and affecti