out language, she was talking about whining. And she said that whining is like a form of self-validation or a seeking of self-validation. So I can be like, isn't this shitty that my parents don't feel well and I'm like tired. And you could be like, it sure is Vanessa. And I'm like, ah, myself got validated. Right. So I don't know what it is, but for the first time, I'm starting to have like such a keen awareness of it. Like, look at the choice you're making. See, I think what you were saying earlier was important, Brooke. Like there was a stage, it wasn't a choice. There was so much density, so much patterning that the only thing I could do was turn to it, meet it and bring love. Right.	091dfb22-ea64-4f44-809d-339bf85f7b26	vanessa
